course: dictionary
lesson: 2671
title: Diagonal lines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diagonal is a slanting line. It is not straight across and not straight up and down. Think of a ramp, or the line you would walk if you went from one corner of a square tile floor to the opposite corner.
explain: In geometry, a diagonal is a straight line that joins two corners of a shape that are not next to each other. A square has 4 corners, and the two diagonals cross in the middle. «Draw the diagonal» means draw that line from one corner to the opposite one.
explain: Context helps you spot the word. «A square frame can squash sideways, but a diagonal brace makes a square strong.» The brace is the slanting stick that stops the frame wobbling. Diagonal is the word for that slanting direction.
fact: A diagonal is a straight line that joins two corners that are not next to each other.
fact: «Diagonal» describes a slanting direction, not straight across or straight up.
fact: A square and a rectangle each have 2 diagonals.
fact: A pentagon has 5 diagonals, and a triangle has none.
fact: «Diagonally» means in a slanting direction, from one corner towards the opposite one, as the bishop moves in chess.
exercise: «Adding a diagonal strut to a square frame divides it into two triangles.» What does diagonal mean here? | Down the side of the frame | Straight across the top | *Slanting, from one corner towards the opposite one | Round and curved
exercise: How many diagonals does a square have? | 0 | 4 | 1 | *2
exercise: Which shape has no diagonals? | *Triangle | Rectangle | Pentagon | Square
test: How many diagonals does a pentagon have? | 2 | 0 | *5 | 3
test: In chess, which way does the bishop move? | Straight across | Up and down | In a circle | *Diagonally
exam: «The corners were diagonally opposite.» What does diagonally opposite mean? | Two corners right next to each other on the same side | The middle point of the shape | *Two corners that are not next to each other, joined by a diagonal | Two corners on the same straight edge
